            <h3>Early and Late Train Availability</h3>
            <p>First train (Carolinian) typically departs in the morning, making daytime travel practical. Last train (Crescent) departs in the evening, allowing flexibility for late departures and overnight travel. Both trains are direct services, minimizing travel complexity.</p>
            <h3>What This Means for Travelers</h3>
            <p>You can plan your journey around two distinct windows - daytime or overnight. The morning train helps maximize daytime at your destination upon arrival. The evening option is ideal for saving on accommodation and arriving refreshed. The limited schedule means booking in advance is strongly recommended to secure your preferred departure.</p>
            <h2>Understanding the Route Geography</h2>
            <p>The journey begins in Charlotte and moves northward through the Carolinas, passing through Virginia's Piedmont region, Washington D.C., Baltimore, and into Pennsylvania. It passes through regions known for rolling countryside, historic Civil War sites, and the Chesapeake Bay watershed. As you approach Philadelphia, the scenery shifts to the urban landscape of the Delaware Valley.</p>
